	<p>
		Baseball is notoriously known for its unpredictable nature and shifts in momentum that can occur at 
		any moment during games. With this idea we <strong>intend to capture the knowns and discover part of 
		the unknowns.</strong> I'm personally proud of the ability to predict the attendance of guests to ball parks 
		allowing management to prepare and additionally scale their pricing for improved revenue. 
		Additionally it’s an amazing opportunity to map out and deploy code that can be used by the masses. 
		<strong>- Rodolfo</strong>
	</p>

	<p>
		Our project is unique because it combines MLB attendance, ballpark characteristics, weather, scheduling, 
		and matchup data into one interactive analytics application. Rather than only displaying baseball statistics, 
		it addresses a real-world business problem by identifying which game conditions may create higher demand for 
		tickets. The project <strong>would be useful to teams for planning promotions, evaluating attendance trends, and 
		supporting ticket-pricing decisions</strong>, while also demonstrating practical database design, query optimization, 
		and web application development.
		<strong>- Kyle</strong>
	</p>

